  "body": "https://groups.google.com/d/msg/mozilla.dev.platform/YFRTGKaY5-g/NzJXAdxFAAAJ contains interesting discussion where Firefox is trying to figure out which tokens they \"support\".\n\nThe intent of the current spec is that the following are the only _possible_ supported tokens, among those defined in HTML:\n- `link`:  alternate, icon, pingback, prefetch, stylesheet and next\n- `a`/`area`:  noreferrer, noopener, and prefetch\n\nIn particular, Firefox has concluded that they support `search` for `<link>`, but the current spec doesn't allow that. Also, they support `next` for `<link>` as an alias for `prefetch` (#1183), but pending the outcome of that discussion, we might want to support it on `<a>`/`<area>` as well.\n\nMaybe the idea of \"possible supported tokens\" is not a good one, and we should just tell UAs to include everything that they implement special code for. Thoughts?\n",
